  "abstract": "Covers the W3C Web Content Accessibility Guidelines at WCAG 2.2 (W3C Recommendation, 12 December 2024 edition): conformance levels A, AA and AAA, the five conformance requirements, accessibility support, conformance claims and partial conformance statements, the success criteria under the four principles (perceivable, operable, understandable, robust), the nine criteria added in 2.2 and the removal of 4.1.1 Parsing, and testing with the informative Understanding, Techniques and Test Rules documents. Version lines: WCAG 2.2 is current, WCAG 2.1 (6 May 2025 edition) is supported, WCAG 2.0 (11 December 2008) is legacy, and the WCAG 3.0 Working Draft (10 September 2026) is tracked as a preview, with upgrade steps from 2.0 and 2.1. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the version lines, conformance, perceivable and operable criteria, understandable and robust criteria, and testing.",
